# Workspace outbound email

Use the configured Workspace SMTP relay for eligible managed Group senders. A new
Group does not require another Gmail Send mail as alias when relay verification
accepts it. Preserve the existing Gmail exceptions; do not remove aliases or
substitute another From address to work around the Gmail alias limit.

- Verify the Group, app-manager membership, active tenant sender identity, domain
  ownership and relay readiness. Never reactivate a deliberately disabled sender.
- The backend and relay service must agree on domain mode, approved domains and
  administrator confirmation. Creating a Group does not authorize its domain.
  Preserve existing IAM, TLS, static egress and Gmail sender pins during changes.
- Appointment reminders use `notifications@auricwell.com` / `AuricWell
  Notifications`. Keep appointment sender configuration separate from account mail.
- Provider-authored cancellation notices use the configured work mailbox resolver.
  For Workspace SSO users this selects tenant `messages@`; Reply-To is the
  provider's work email and support is copied. Preserve the envelope through
  approval/retry and use the server-validated cancellation context.
- School waitlist-to-active/provider-assignment status notices go to the school
  and assigned provider. Do not add automatic family assignment notices. The
  withdrawn `school_family_status_update` template must remain blocked on retry.
- The separate provider opt-in School Contact Plan is still QA-only. Preserve its
  production hold and future-assignment cutoff; the presence of its source code
  does not establish production readiness or authorize opting providers in.
- People Operations submission notices use the explicitly selected, verified
  tenant sender and reviewed staff recipients. ITSCO's dedicated SMTP Group is
  `peopleops-notifications@itsco.health`, with Reply-To `PO@itsco.health`.
  Preserve the existing `PO@` and `messages@` Gmail routes. Enabling this sender
  must not enable notice settings or replay historical submissions.
- Current affiliated guardian contacts remain eligible for operational notices
  even when login/portal access is disabled or pending. Do not grant portal rights.
  Respect actual revoked/no-contact relationships and explicit notification declines.
- Reminder-only email preferences and `NOREMIND` stop reminders. They do not stop
  signed cancellation or genuine schedule-change notices. Preserve separate global,
  confidential-contact and schedule-change choices.
- Verify readiness without sending DATA/mail. Actual notices require the intended
  reviewed workflow; reopening a completed cancellation must not silently resend it.

See [Platform Email Setup](../../docs/PLATFORM_EMAIL_SETUP.md) for relay settings.
